t I risk getting called by any pair (which might be checking to induce a bluff).\nIf I check, I get to see a showdown for free. Since the pot is minimal and it is the first hand of a 20-hand match, preserving chips and taking the showdown value with Q-high is the most prudent play. I have enough showdown value to win a fair percentage of the time against a random checking range without risking more chips.\n\nReason: My hand has marginal showdown value (Queen-high kicker to the board pair). The opponent has shown passivity by checking every street. Betting is unlikely to get value from worse hands and risks being called by better hands. Checking guarantees a showdown for the current pot size without additional risk.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
