isky given the flush heavy board. Betting builds the pot and charges draws. A bet size of roughly the pot (200 chips) is appropriate to deny equity to draws and get value from top pairs.\n\nReason: I have a very strong hand (Three of a Kind) on the turn. The opponent has shown passivity (checking twice post-flop), suggesting they do not have a flush or a strong hand. To maximize value and protect against river draws, I should bet rather than check. A bet of 200 (approx pot size) is standard to build the pot and extract value from worse hands like Top Pair (Kings) or draws.\n\nAnswer: 200'}
